<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Protection Warrior</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria, your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit and 15% Expertise. Keep in mind that some abilities, such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei racial Heroic Presence, will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your attacks will no longer miss Raid bosses. We prioritize Hit in our gearing, as even though it scales linearly to Expertise. Some abilities, like <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=6343/thunder-clap">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_thunderclap.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thunder Clap</span></a>, can miss but can't be dodged or parried.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>Expertise was changed to no longer grant reduction to <i>both</i> the target's ability to dodge <i>and</i> parry. When reaching 7.5% Expertise, you will have removed the boss's chance to dodge, but their chance to parry will remain unchanged. You'll need an additional 7.5% Expertise to eliminate their chance to parry (15% total). <br/>
<br/>This means that while tanking a target, there is effectively no "soft cap" where Expertise starts dropping off in value. However, as you're not always dealing damage to a target head-on, it's still worth thinking about Expertise in terms of a soft cap and hard cap. It's worth noting that if Shield Slam and Revenge is dodged or parried, they grant no Rage.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Protection Warrior</span></h2>Your gems will alternate depending on what you and your raid prioritize. We generally have 3 different playstyles (<i>Offensive</i>, <i>Balanced</i>, and <i>Defensive</i>), and below you'll find the appropriate gems for each playstyle. We generally opt to socket for the socket bonus, but if the bonus does not offer an attractive bonus, then opt for the<b> main gem</b> of each category. <br/>
<br/>
<b>
<span class="q5">Legendary Meta Gem:</span></b> In Phase 3 of Mists of Pandaria, we get access to two new meta gems that provide far greater utility than the normal meta gems. <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95344/indomitable-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Indomitable Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indomitable Primal Diamond</span></a> and <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Capacitive Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitive Primal Diamond</span></a> are the two we can realistically use, and for most people, it should not be much of a choice. <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95344/indomitable-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Indomitable Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indomitable Primal Diamond</span></a> provides the most utility overall with an outrageously high uptime, north of 50%. <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Capacitive Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitive Primal Diamond</span></a> does scale with Vengeance and generally provides a 5-6% damage boost. <br/>
<br/>
